<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.75%" pitch="-2.60%">
            When you pass through the waters, I will be with you.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Through the rivers, they shall not overwhelm you.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            When you walk through fire you shall not be burned, and the flame shall not consume you.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Notice the word. Not around the waters. Not lifted above the fire. Through.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            This is not a promise that the hard things will be removed from your path. It is something deeper. It is a promise of presence inside the hard thing. God does not stand at the edge and call to you from safe ground. He enters the water with you.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            There are seasons that feel like flood. Circumstances that rise faster than you can respond to them. Grief that comes in waves. Anxiety that will not stay still. The feeling of being in over your head, of the current being stronger than you are.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            And God says: I will be with you.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Not I will watch from the bank. Not I will be nearby if you call loud enough. I will be with you. Present. In it. Holding ground beside you.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            They shall not overwhelm you.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            That word — overwhelm — means to be swept away. Drowned. Lost in it. And God says: no. The waters may rise. The river may run fast. But they will not take you under. They will not have the final word. Because I am with you in the water.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            The fire is the same. When you walk through fire — not if, but when — you shall not be burned. The flame has no power over what God has claimed.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            Whatever you have been passing through, you have not been passing through it alone.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            He was there in the water.
            <break time="500ms"/>
            He was there in the fire.
            <break time="500ms"/>
            He is here now.
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
